<h2 id="infoSection">MrMine item info (<a href="https://archive.knarcraft.net/Scripts/Tools/Mr-Mine-Save-Editor#editSection">edit</a>)</h2>
<h3>Scientist info</h3>
<p>Scientist level: Minutes excavated / 360 + 1.</p>
<p>Time until death: How long to excavate for before killing the scientist. If it's 0, the scientist won't die.</p>
<p>A scientist must have either an active excavation or two excavation choices. If the duration of an excavation is 0, the excavation slot is set to empty.</p>
<h3>Trading</h3>
<p>Trading is quite statically coded and which values are valid depends on other values. Valid trades are defined in tradingpost.js in the variable traders.</p>
<p>Payment subtype only matters for ore payment type and is ore id as defined in the mineral list down below.</p>
<p>Reward subtypes are a bit more complicated.
    For ore reward type, reward subtype must be a mineral in the mineral list.
    For chest reward type, reward subtype must be 0 for wooden chest or 1 for gold chest.
    For relic reward type, valid values are defined in the relic list.
    For other reward types, -1 seems to be the only valid value.
    Buffs and blueprints seem to still be unfinished and will probably be properly defined in the future.</p>
<p>Trade amounts should be 1 for chests, relics, blueprints and buffs, but can by any positive value for money and minerals.</p>
<h3>Chests</h3>
<p>Chests spawn every 30 seconds and each 10km can contain one chest, and is rolled independently. A chest will despawn after 1hr-2.4hr.
    Chests will overwrite other chests when spawning. This can make another chest disappear after just 30 seconds, including gold chests.
    If a chest will spawn, that chest has a 1 in 158 chance of spawning as a gold chest. Except for rewards, the two chest types behave the same.</p>
